      "writtenOn": "2026-05-21T18:11:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] Using `CONFIG_ROLLBACK_SIZE` to cover both `rollback0` and `rollback1` in a single region is efficient for ARMv8-M. However, this assumes they are always contiguous in memory. While this is likely true for current boards, adding a compile-time check or explicitly including both in the array (even if they result in one region if contiguous) would be safer.",
